<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Mary Borji - Formal Complaint Letter</title>
  <style>
    body{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#111827;line-height:1.48;margin:42px;font-size:13.5px}
    .subject{font-weight:bold;color:#003f88;margin:18px 0}.box{border-left:4px solid #0052a4;background:#eef6ff;padding:10px 12px;margin:14px 0}
    li{margin:5px 0}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <p>[DATE]</p>
  <p>
    The Directors / Complaints Department<br>
    Protect Insulation Services Ltd<br>
    [Company Address TBC]
  </p>
  <p><strong>BY POST AND EMAIL IF AVAILABLE</strong></p>
  <p>Dear Sirs,</p>

  <p class="subject">
    Re: Formal Complaint - Spray Foam Loft Insulation at 11 Richland Road, Liverpool, L13 7BN<br>
    Client: Mrs Mary Borji<br>
    Installation date: 18/02/2021<br>
    Installation price: GBP 7,350<br>
    Funding route: Green Homes Scheme / original grant voucher available
  </p>

  <p>We write on behalf of Mrs Mary Borji regarding spray foam loft insulation supplied and/or installed at the above property.</p>
  <p>Our client understands that the works were connected with Protect Insulation Services Ltd and funded through the Green Homes Scheme. Mrs Borji holds the original grant voucher and further supporting documents can be provided as required.</p>
  <p>Mrs Borji's position is that she was not made aware of the potential structural, mortgage, property value, roof-access or future repair implications associated with spray foam loft insulation at the point of sale or installation.</p>
  <p>Mrs Borji also complains that the spray foam installation was carried out negligently and to an unacceptable standard. A subsequent inspection by a local roofing company identified excessive humidity levels within the loft and extensive deterioration of the timber roof structure. Mrs Borji has photographic evidence of the damage.</p>
  <p>Owing to the severity of the deterioration, a substantial section of the roof required replacement in or around January 2026 at a cost of GBP 5,800. Spray foam insulation remains present on the loft floor, joists and a dividing brick wall.</p>

  <p>Our client's complaint is that you failed to:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Carry out a proper roof suitability and ventilation assessment before installation.</li>
    <li>Warn Mrs Borji of the potential risks of spray foam insulation, including moisture retention, ventilation restriction, timber deterioration, mortgage/sale concerns and future roof repair complications.</li>
    <li>Ensure the product and installation method were suitable for the property.</li>
    <li>Install the product to an acceptable standard and in a way that did not cause or contribute to property damage.</li>
    <li>Provide adequate written warnings, aftercare guidance, warranty information and complaint routes.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>As a result, Mrs Borji has suffered loss and damage. The losses currently identified include, but may not be limited to:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Original spray foam installation cost / grant-funded works: GBP 7,350.</li>
    <li>Roof replacement / remedial roofing costs: GBP 5,800.</li>
    <li>Further removal, remediation, survey, inspection or repair costs to be confirmed.</li>
    <li>Consequential loss, inconvenience and distress arising from the defective installation and damage.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="box"><strong>Requested response:</strong> Please treat this letter as a formal complaint and provide a full written response within 14 days.</div>

  <p>Please confirm within 14 days:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Whether you accept responsibility for the sale and/or installation.</li>
    <li>Whether you carried out a pre-installation roof suitability, moisture and ventilation assessment.</li>
    <li>Whether you hold survey notes, photographs, installation records, method statements, risk assessments or call recordings.</li>
    <li>What warnings were given to Mrs Borji about moisture, timber deterioration, roof access, mortgageability, saleability and future roof repairs.</li>
    <li>Whether any warranty, guarantee, insurance-backed guarantee, Green Homes Scheme obligation or approved-installer requirement applies.</li>
    <li>Whether you will reimburse Mrs Borji for the installation cost and all reasonably incurred remedial losses.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>If you deny liability, please provide your full written reasons and copies of all documents you rely upon.</p>
  <p>Please preserve all records relating to this matter, including sales notes, survey records, photographs, contracts, grant paperwork, warranties, payment records, installation documents and internal correspondence.</p>
  <p>If we do not receive a satisfactory response, Mrs Borji reserves the right to escalate the matter through all available legal, regulatory, warranty, scheme, insurance or complaint routes.</p>

  <p>Yours faithfully,</p>
  <p>[NAME]<br>For and on behalf of Mrs Mary Borji<br>[CONTACT DETAILS]</p>
</body>
</html>
